dist/
*.log
.DS_Store

# app declared-store / worktrees created while dogfooding THIS repo in the app
/.worktrees.places.json
/.worktrees/
# the backups `worktrees sync pull` leaves in the tree it mirrored over
/.worktrees-sync/

# design-review artifacts (browser harness screenshots + playwright output)
.playwright-mcp/
/baseline-*.png
/redesign-*.png
/ctx-*.png

# IDE
.idea/

# Rust workspace build artifacts (shared root target/ now that app/ joined the workspace)
/target/

# planning-with-files working docs — the plan for the CURRENT work stream, kept
# local; at close-out they're tarballed into docs/sessions/<date>-<slug>/
# next to the session summary (see .claude/skills/close-out). (DESIGN.md +
# MIGRATION.md are tracked design docs; these are scratch/working memory.)
#
# Two layouts, both ignored. The three root files are the original flat layout.
# `.planning/` is the directory form, and it is also where `worktrees new`
# writes an agent's brief — BRIEF_PATH in crates/worktrees-core/src/ops.rs,
# whose doc comment says this working dir is one "every repo of ours already
# gitignores". That was true of our other repos and quietly false of this one
# until this line existed, so a brief written into a worktree OF worktrees
# would have shown up as an untracked file with nothing to explain it.
/task_plan.md
/findings.md
/progress.md
.planning/

# session screenshots belong in ~/.cache/worktrees/<project>/<worktree>/ — these
# patterns are the safety net for strays in the repo root
/nav-*.png
/upd-*.png
/plumb-*.png
/align-*.png
/theme-*.png
/Screenshot*.png

# local Jekyll builds of docs/ (the GitHub Pages site)
_site/
.sass-cache/
